// The tabular (arithmetic) Hijri calendar, scaled to the 120-day game year
// (ADR-0007). No hisab, no rukyat: a pure function of the day counter.
//
// The real calendar has 12 months of 29/30 days (354) plus 11 leap days in
// every 30-year cycle. Scaled by 120/365, the months become 9 or 10 days and
// the common year 116 days, so the Hijri year walks ~4 days earlier against
// the mangsa every game year, as Ramadan does in life. Leap years add one day
// to month 12 (Dzulhijjah), exactly where the real calendar adds it.
//
// Month lengths are spread evenly (floor(116·m/12) steps), so Ramadan (month
// 9) is 10 days. GDD §10's "30 days" is the real-world length, not game days.
//
// `epoch` is the Hijri date of game day 0 (the arrival). Chosen so the first
// Ramadan lands in musim hujan of year 1; it is a design knob, not a fact.
{
  monthDays: [9, 10, 10, 9, 10, 10, 9, 10, 10, 9, 10, 10],
  cycleYears: 30,
  // Positions within the 30-year cycle that are leap years (the most common
  // tabular variant; others move the 15th/16th-year leap by one).
  leapYears: [2, 5, 7, 10, 13, 16, 18, 21, 24, 26, 29],
  epoch: { year: 1448, month: 1, day: 1 },
}
